P9 includes/qa/   # QA harness: loopback requests to the site's own pages, run from WP-CLI or the admin QA screen only. includes/qa is excluded from the release zip by .distignore.
S4 includes/class-recount.php   # What is left interpolates only internal table names (table()) and a range built with %d and (int) casts; the member-id list is bound through prepare(). No request value reaches the SQL.
P9 includes/captcha/   # Captcha verification is the request: the form (register, post, reply) is accepted or refused on the provider's answer, so it cannot be handed to a background job. A timeout fails closed.
P9 includes/integrations/class-companion-installer.php   # An admin clicks Install on a companion plugin; the download and the single error-diagnosis probe are that click's work, never a visitor's request.
P9 includes/adapters/class-ollama-ai-adapter.php   # The adapter only runs when Jetonomy Pro's AI client calls it: from Action Scheduler (summaries, batch review, digests) or from a user-initiated action whose answer is the response. Free itself never calls it.
P9 includes/services/links/   # Link preview is a REST call the composer makes while the member types: rate-limited per user, cached, and its answer IS the response, so it cannot be deferred.
P9 includes/class-embeds.php   # wp_oembed_get() resolves a pasted URL once and the result (and a miss) is cached per URL for a day, so only the first view of a NEW link makes a provider request. Known ceiling: that first view waits on the provider (WordPress default 5 s timeout). A later release can resolve embeds from Action Scheduler at save time; not done here.
